        role: "Parks department supervisor",
        exam: [.direct("What is your role?", "\"I supervise the town's parks department, including inspections, repairs, and reports of damage in our parks.\""), .direct("What did you find at the park?", "\"A slide had been cut with a saw and a sign was scorched, causing about fifteen hundred dollars of damage.\""), .direct("What did the tool marks show?", "\"The cuts had a distinctive blade pattern, and the State Crime Lab matched it to a hacksaw blade owned by {DL}.\""), .direct("How did you connect the blade to {DL}?", "\"A deputy had recovered it in the earlier case, and its markings matched the marks at the park.\""), .direct("What did a neighbor report?", "\"Two teens leaving the park at night after hearing a loud noise, though not who they were.\""), .direct("What did {DL} say?", "\"{D.He} said the tool was lost in the earlier case and hasn't been in {D.his} possession since.\""), .cross("The blade matches a type many people own?", "\"The lab said the marks match that blade, but it's a common type.\""), .cross("You didn't see {DL} at the park?", "\"No. I only know what the lab found.\""), .cross("The teens were not identified?", "\"No, the neighbor could only say two young people left.\""), .cross("Someone else could have used the same blade?", "\"It's possible if it was found or stolen, though the lab matched this specific one.\""), .cross("The tool was in evidence from the earlier case?", "\"It was collected then. I can't say whether it was returned afterward.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} damaged a park again.", "A lost tool."),
        allocution: "\"I'm sorry for what happened to that playground. The saw blade matched a tool I lost during the earlier case, and I never touched that slide or sign. I've been in this courtroom before, and I know it's easy to point at me. I hope the court looks at the facts.\"",
        truths: ("The tool was returned to {DL}.", "The marks matched a hacksaw sold at every hardware store in the county."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you cut the slide?", "\"No. I didn't go near that park. The hacksaw was taken from me after the earlier case.\""), .direct("What happened to the tool?", "\"The deputies kept it, or lost it. I never got it back, and I haven't owned one like it since.\""), .direct("Where were you that night?", "\"At home, mostly, and I may have gone out for a short walk. I didn't go to a park.\""), .direct("Do you know who did it?", "\"No. I've heard that teens hang around there. I don't know who was involved.\""), .direct("What did you do when the deputy asked?", "\"I told {OFF.him} I'd lost the tool, and I let {OFF.him} check my garage.\""), .direct("What would you tell the town?", "\"I'm sorry for the damage to the park. I didn't do it, and I hope the court finds who did.\""), .cross("You had been in this courtroom before, hadn't you?", "\"Yes, and I realize how this looks to the court. I'm telling the truth.\""), .cross("The lab matched your hacksaw blade?", "\"So the lab says. If it was lost, someone else must have found it.\""), .cross("You can't prove the tool was lost?", "\"Only by the record of the earlier case. I never got it back.\""), .cross("You've damaged property before?", "\"Yes, in the earlier case. I've learned from it and haven't done it since.\""), .cross("You'll cooperate with the town?", "\"Yes. I'll help in any way, and I'll pay my share if the court says I should.\"")],
        openings: ("A slide at another park was cut with a saw and a sign was scorched, about $1,500 of damage, and blade marks on the slide match {D}'s hacksaw. A neighbor saw two teens leave the park, and {DL} had faced this court in {PRIORDATE} over {PRIOR}.", "The defense will say {D}'s hacksaw was lost during the earlier case and that anyone could have found and used it. A tool mark does not prove who held the tool."),
        closings: ("The blade marks match {D}'s hacksaw, the damage came after {PRIOR}, and {DL} knew what that tool had done before. A neighbor saw two teens leave the park, and {D} is the one whose tool matches.", "A lost tool can end up in anyone's hands. The State must prove {D} was the one who cut the slide, and marks alone cannot say who."),
        timeline: [(0, "The park is damaged."), (1, "Staff report it.")],
