        openings: ("A masked man came into a different store, put his hand in a pocket as if he had a weapon, and told {V} to give him the cash. A cap matches one seized earlier from {D}, and {DL} had faced this court in {PRIORDATE} over {PRIOR}.", "The defense will say caps like this are common and thousands of men own one, and that a cap is not an identification. {D} was not the man behind the mask, and nothing but a hat says otherwise."),
